Decide the language question the way the ADR asked to be asked, and record what that actually cost

ADR 0003 refused to pick a stack and named the evidence that would settle it: the same
vertical slice built twice, an evaluation harness in each, a deliberate 2am breakage, an
honest familiarity score, and a contractor price check. It set a deadline of "before the
first line of application code" and warned that the alternative was deciding by accident.

Both spikes exist and are committed here, dependencies gitignored, source intact. The
decision is TypeScript on Node, and ADR 0005 records it with the reasoning attached:
the TypeScript spike expressed the two constraints ADR 0003 called disqualifying as
structural facts rather than conventions -- a workspace scope that cannot be built without
a workspace and has no raw database handle, and a confirmation proof the tracker writer
demands, so "no write without a human" is a compile error rather than a review comment.

What that ADR also records is where the method was not followed. The Python spike never
wrote its measurements file, so the line-and-hours comparison the ADR asked for does not
exist and the two were compared by reading them. The familiarity score was never taken.
No contractor was asked to price a second tracker integration. Those are written down as
skipped rather than quietly dropped, because an ADR that only lists the evidence that
agreed with it is an advertisement.

The evaluation-harness test, which 0003 called decisive, was answered late but honestly:
it exists, it scores a 217-example golden set across a threshold sweep, and it earned its
keep immediately by proving that a family of confident false positives could not be fixed
by any threshold. The prompt changed instead, and detection precision went from 81.0% to
100.0% at 95.8% recall.

Also here: the implementation brief the application was actually built from, and a note in
the README that this repository is now the specification rather than the whole story. The
application lives in Seros-LLC/seros-app. ADR 0004 stays proposed, because no model vendor
has been chosen and pretending otherwise would repeat the mistake 0003 was written to stop.
